\ Dogfood: `core::bool`'s `if`/`unless`, exercised through `hosted::testing`.
\ Neither `Bool` nor `Ordering` has an `Ord` impl, so this suite leans on
\ `expect` alone (R5.1): each assertion's arm is chosen so the dispatch under
\ test only reads back `True` when it picked the right branch.

import: core::prelude * ;
import: hosted::testing | expect | ;

: main ( -- )
  True ~[ True ] ~[ False ] if "if runs the first arm when the condition is true" expect
  False ~[ False ] ~[ True ] if "if runs the second arm when the condition is false" expect
  True ~[ False ] ~[ True ] unless "unless runs the second arm when the condition is true" expect
  False ~[ True ] ~[ False ] unless "unless runs the first arm when the condition is false" expect ;
